{"id":"G2062","lemma":"ἑρπετόν","transliteration":"herpeton","sayIt":"herpeton","language":"Greek","partOfSpeech":"noun, neuter","gloss":"reptile","meaning":"ἑρπετόν, -οῦ, τό\n(ἕρπω, to crawl), [in LXX chiefly for רֶמֶשׂ, שֶׁרֶץ ;]\na creeping thing, reptile: Act.10:12 11:6, Rom.1:23, Jas.3:7.†\n(AS)","glosses":["reptiles"],"count":4,"occurrences":[{"chapterId":"act-10","v":12,"renderings":{"bsb":"reptiles","kjv":"creeping things"}},{"chapterId":"act-11","v":6,"renderings":{"bsb":"reptiles","kjv":"creeping things"}},{"chapterId":"rom-1","v":23,"renderings":{"bsb":"reptiles"}},{"chapterId":"jas-3","v":7,"renderings":{"bsb":"reptiles","kjv":"of serpents"}}],"elsewhere":[{"ref":"Acts 10:12","note":"in which were all kinds of four-footed animals of the earth, wild animals, reptiles, and birds of the sky.","source":"web"},{"ref":"Romans 1:23","note":"and traded the glory of the incorruptible God for the likeness of an image of corruptible man, and of birds, four-footed animals, and creeping things.","source":"web"},{"ref":"James 3:7","note":"For every kind of animal, bird, creeping thing, and sea creature, is tamed, and has been tamed by mankind;","source":"web"}],"related":[{"id":"G20620","lemma":"κυλίκιον","transliteration":"kulikion","gloss":"small cup"},{"id":"G20621","lemma":"κυνάμυια","transliteration":"kunamuia","gloss":"shameless fly"},{"id":"G20622","lemma":"κυνήγιον","transliteration":"kunēgion","gloss":"prey"},{"id":"G20623","lemma":"κυοφορία","transliteration":"kuophoria","gloss":"pregnancy"},{"id":"G20624","lemma":"κύπρος","transliteration":"kupros","gloss":"a measure of corn"},{"id":"G20625","lemma":"κυρία","transliteration":"kuria","gloss":"possession, control"},{"id":"G20626","lemma":"κωλῆ","transliteration":"kōlē","gloss":"membrum virile"},{"id":"G20627","lemma":"κωνώπιον","transliteration":"kōnōpion","gloss":"cōnōpēum"}],"sources":["STEPBible TBESH/TBESG lexicon (CC BY 4.0)","STEPBible TAHOT/TAGNT tagged text (CC BY 4.0)"]}